dirac-link-9222b6e7.conceptual_definition:
The Dirac link, also known as the Dirac quantization condition, is a fundamental result in theoretical physics that postulates a necessary condition for the existence of both electric and magnetic charges. It states that if a magnetic monopole exists, then electric charge must be quantized. Specifically, the product of the smallest unit of electric charge (\(q_e
